ience of the reader.\n       See United States v. Detroit ", "type": "combined-opinion"}, {"author_id": null, "cites": [85953, 90510, 90965, 94619, 95660, 95758, 97114, 97639, 97976, 98312, 98512, 99192, 100597, 101215, 102439, 106321, 107042, 108755, 108812, 110962, 111106, 111411, 112822, 118166, 508922, 586427, 1189024, 3187496, 3800210, 3810210, 3822004, 3828383, 3831909, 3832056, 3832674, 3834260, 5142637, 5142716, 5158122, 8756805, 8768166, 9226134, 9416337, 9419634, 9423720, 9426014, 9426745, 9428044, 9428242, 9431834, 9432029, 9432941, 9538042, 9789835, 9842054, 9879185, 9887864], "download_url": null, "id": 9889205, "joined_by_ids": [], "local_path": null, "meta": {"timestamp": "2025-11-29T05:01:42.184447Z", "date_created": "2023-10-06T20:26:58.936495Z"}, "ordering_key": 1, "per_curiam": false, "sha1": "", "snippet": "\nJustice GORSUCH delivered the opinion of the Court.\n*2459On the far end of the Trail of Tears was a promise. Forced to leave their ancestral lands in Georgia and Alabama, the Creek Nation received assurances that their new lands in the West would be secure forever. In exchange for ceding \"all their land, East of the Mississippi river,\" the ", "type": "lead-opinion"}, {"author_id": null, "cites": [98886, 102505, 111106, 932061, 3187496, 9331386, 9789835, 9842054, 9842121, 9879185], "download_url": null, "id": 9889206, "joined_by_ids": [], "local_path": null, "meta": {"timestamp": "2025-11-29T05:01:22.796892Z", "date_created": "2023-10-06T20:26:58.957291Z"}, "ordering_key": 2, "per_curiam": false, "sha1": "", "snippet": "\nJustice THOMAS, dissenting.\nI agree with THE CHIEF JUSTICE that the former Creek Nation Reservation was disestablished at statehood and Oklahoma therefore has jurisdiction to prosecute petitioner for sexually assaulting his wife's granddaughter. Ante , at 2482 - 2483 (dissenting opinion). I write separately to note an additional defect in the Court's decision: It reverses a state-court judgment that it has no jurisdictio", "type": "dissent"}], "panel_ids": [], "panel_names": [], "posture": "", "procedural_history": "", "scdb_id": "", "sibling_ids": [4547014, 9889205, 9889206], "source": "CU", "status": "Published", "suitNature": "", "syllabus": ""}, {"absolute_url": "/opinion/9365269/mcgirt-v-oklahoma/", "attorney": "", "caseName": "McGirt v. Oklahoma", "caseNameFull": "Jimcy MCGIRT v. OKLAHOMA.", "citation": ["140 S. Ct. 1102", "206 L. Ed. 2d 176"], "citeCount": 0, "cluster_id": 9365269, "court": "Supreme Court of the United States", "court_citation_string": "SCOTUS", "court_id": "scotus", "court_jurisdiction": null, "dateArgued": null, "dateFiled": "2020-02-24", "dateReargued": null, "dateReargumentDenied": null, "docketNumber": "No. 18-9526", "docket_id": 66726651, "judge": "", "lexisCite": "", "meta": {"timestamp": "2024-06-23T00:57:38.522009Z", "date_created": "2023-01-13T06:53:25.793340Z", "score": {"bm25": 240.03378}}, "neutralCite": "", "non_participating_judge_ids": [], "opinions": [{"author_id": null, "cites": [], "download_url": null, "id": 9360745, "joined_by_ids": [], "local_path": null, "meta": {"timestamp": "2024-06-25T07:27:22.417026Z", "date_created": "2023-01-13T06:53:25.800362Z"}, "ordering_key": null, "per_curiam": false, "sha1": "", "snippet": "Motion of petitioner to dispense with printing the joint appendix granted.", "type": "lead-opinion"}], "panel_ids": [], "panel_names": [], "posture": "", "procedural_history": "", "scdb_id": "", "sibling_ids": [9360745], "source": "U", "status": "Published", "suitNature": "", "syllabus": ""}, {"absolute_url": "/opinion/9366288/mcgirt-v-oklahoma/", "attorney": "", "caseName": "McGirt v. Oklahoma", "caseNameFull": "Jimcy MCGIRT v. OKLAHOMA.", "citation": ["140 S. Ct. 2562", "206 L. Ed. 2d 494"], "citeCount": 0, "cluster_id": 9366288, "court": "Supreme Court of the United States", "court_citation_string": "SCOTUS", "court_id": "scotus", "court_jurisdiction": null, "dateArgued": null, "dateFiled": "2020-03-30", "dateReargued